Package: enterotyperobustness
Type: Package
Title: Sampling-Based Evaluation of Enterotype Assignment Stability (ERP and ERPM)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Irene", "Creus-Marti", role = c("aut")),
    person("Eugeni", "Belda", email = "eugeni.belda@ird.fr", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jean-Daniel", "Zucker", role = "aut"),
    person("Edi", "Prifti", role = "aut"),
    person("Karine", "Clement", role = "aut"))
Description: Two resampling procedures that quantify how stable individual enterotype
    assignments are under Dirichlet Multinomial Mixture (DMM) clustering. The Enterotype
    Robustness Process (ERP) holds an anchor set of samples fixed and varies the clinical
    composition of the samples clustered with them; its size-perturbation variant (ERPM)
    varies the fraction of a cohort that is clustered. Both take a plain abundance matrix
    and sample-ID vectors, so they run on any cohort without shipping the cohort's data.
    Cluster-to-enterotype annotation is available as the original rank heuristic and as
    centroid matching across iterations.
